#
#
#
# Checked by tests/check-exported-symbols.sh: an addition is a deliberate
# The conditional lines at the end name entry points a build has only if
# The library's exported symbol set, one name per line, C-collation sorted.
# The reserved-exception lines at the end name the exports that begin with
# act recorded here in the same commit, and a removal breaks a consumer.
# an underscore. C99 7.1.3 reserves every file-scope identifier that does,
# it was configured for them: each is a display device compiled for one
# name. These four predate the rule and are recorded rather than renamed;
# nor refused. tests/check-device-roster.sh is what holds the device set.
# so exporting one is a collision waiting on a libc that uses the same
# the list may shrink and may not grow.
# windowing system and absent everywhere else. They are neither required
DEBUGLOAD
_currentpoint
_xpost_garbage_diag_verify
_xpost_garbage_diag_xbank
